Z||000016||85ZainoGT||08-18-2001||08:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>Here are the pics... was going to clean them a little, but photoshop wouldn't let me open them? Never had that happen before...?<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mdfiero1.jpg">    <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mdfiero2.jpg">    <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mdfiero3.jpg">    <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mdfiero4.jpg">    <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mdfiero5.jpg">    <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mdfiero6.jpg">    <P>Edit: Fixed images...-RB<P><BR>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 08-17-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I want... where? how much? :::::drooling:::::||||reg||1
Z||000017||b lo 0||08-19-2001||01:22 AM||||Good lord!  You guys like?  They're free!  That's right, FREE!  On a notchback, remove the taillight assembly, then carefully pry open the retaining clips for the lens, and VERY CAREFULLY peel off the clear lens cover.  It's held on with silicone adhesive.  When the cover is off, remove both the red and clear grille/lens assemblies, then just snap the clear outer cover back on the bucket and PRESTO!  Clear tails!  Easiest mod I've ever done.  I was looking at a fastback tonight and I think it could be done, if someone wants to send me a broken fastback taillight, I'll try.  Only problem, the red bulbs are $15 (!) a set (6) at Pep Boys.  The people who were driving behind me tonight (friends) said the brake lights were REALLY bright.  And man, the reverse lamps are FANTASTIC!  It's like I have fog lights on the back of my car!  Lots of people like them.  Mine look like QwikGTA's, only the center section is black like MinnGreen's.  Ronnie got a chance to see the finished driver's side complete with the '85 GT trademark smoke covers today.  The pass. side has a cracked lens and is not done, but Albatross is helping me out there.  I'll have pics soon.||||reg||1
Z||000018||btoth||08-19-2001||12:07 PM||||From what I've been told, as long as the bulbs are the correct color (as mentioned above) <B>and</B> you have red reflectors somewhere on the back of your car (which it looks like you do), you're fine.<P>The problem some people have with them is that modern cars have the reflectors as part of the tail-light themselves and when they switch to the clear ones, they get rid of the reflectors, too.||||reg||1
Z||000019||MD_Fiero||08-19-2001||02:31 PM||||Well, for us...our housing is our reflective pieces....<P>as for the one wanting the tail light mod i made.. do a simple project such as above...take off the lens..and pull out the color pieces...etc....then go to a auto shop, or better yet.....a trailer tractor supply store...find lense's that you think would fit...and u could use super glue, or hot glue gun(like i did) and did a very clean job...and damnnnn, these things are bright!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Good Luck, and post pics!||||reg||1
Z||000020||MD_Fiero||08-19-2001||02:32 PM||||BTW...thank's for posting my pix mingreen!<P>really appreciated=)||||reg||1
Z||000021||Pontiaddict||08-19-2001||06:31 PM||||If i remember right, you're supposed to have at least 2 square inches of red reflective material visible from the back of the car. You have that with the 2 reflectors in the bumper so you can have just the colored bulbs in the lenses. Other cars have the reflectors as part of the original lenses and you have to have clear lenses with red reflective material somewhere on them, like on the new Lightning.<P>Will the black grate pieces fit back into the taillights with the red and clear parts taken out? Or will it just flop around?||||reg||1
