Z||000027||Pontiaddict||08-20-2001||01:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by b lo 0:<BR><B> <BR>The black grates and the color peices are one and the same.  You'd have to make new grates if you want the look.  Sorry   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.  BTW, I recommend cleaning the lens and bucket real good with household cleaner like 409 so it'll look better.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The reason I asked is because on my 84, the pieces were seperate. A friend of mine broke one of my taillights a few years ago, and when I replaced it I took the old one apart just to see how they were made. I think I threw it away afterwards, (maybe it's still out in the shed, I'll have to look tomorrow.) but I remember there being a black plastic grating between the clear plastic covers and the red and clear pieces that went over the lights. Maybe it was an 84 thing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Or my memory is just really bad.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
