Z||000033||Phil||08-20-2001||04:52 PM||||I was just visiting my local speedshop and he showed me a flyer he got from his supplier- stating that clear tail-light lenes are for export use only (not DOT approved). He could return any sets he had for credit. I guess if you still have some red reflective material in the rear you should be OK.||||reg||1
Z||000034||MinnGreenGT||08-20-2001||05:33 PM||||Phil- from what I understand about clear lenses, DOT approved new taillights must have a certain amount of reflector material on them, since newer cars don't have separate rear reflectors- which the Fiero has located in the lower fascia. Shouldn't be any problems!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000035||Simple Fiero||08-20-2001||06:20 PM||||Actually guys it was pretty easy I went into my local walmart and bought some red reflector lenses, cause I heard from my local lordco that you have to have reflective surface up here so I took a chance and bought the reflectors I thought at first they would slide right in but they were a little big so I used a dremel to cut them down, then I was going to use silicone but I had to use glue due to the crap drying time of silicone, it took me about an hr, that is it. and I think they look great. Thanks for the compliments.<BR>THANKS again MinnGreenGT||||reg||1
Z||000036||MinnGreenGT||08-20-2001||09:36 PM||||Simple- No problem...<P>I should be recieving a doner GT Fastback Taillight in the next few days- I'll take it apart and then head down to the local WalMart and look for those reflector-lenses.  What dept did you get them from? Auto or Bikes or ????<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000037||theogre||08-20-2001||09:53 PM||||To answer the orginal question, Just like the headlights, there are legal issues with rear light modification.<P>There is a link in my cave to a good sight about this. He's covering federally ordered recalls on aftermarket rear lights like many of the "ricers" use.<P>The notch back modification above is probably illegal in many areas because it eliminates the reflector. The addon reflector one person above used may not be enough legally. <P>Allot of this is up to local police and how crabby they want to be if you are going to have problems or not on the road. You also have to watch out for state DMV inspections in allot of states. Also keep in mind when you drive away from your local area you could make yourself a ticket magnet.||||reg||1
Z||000038||b lo 0||08-21-2001||12:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B><BR>The notch back modification above is probably illegal in many areas because it eliminates the reflector. The addon reflector one person above used may not be enough legally. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ogre, I hate to go against you, but there was no reflector material removed in the process of modifying the tails.  The reflectors are in the rear fascia, remember?  If it's the reflectors that count, and red bulbs, I shouldn't have a problem.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000039||Simple Fiero||08-21-2001||12:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>Simple- No problem...<P>I should be recieving a doner GT Fastback Taillight in the next few days- I'll take it apart and then head down to the local WalMart and look for those reflector-lenses.  What dept did you get them from? Auto or Bikes or ????<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I got them from the auto area if I remember they were with all the other headlight stuff.<BR>And Ogre you are probably right about the legal issues, but up here in BC, Altezza Style lights are very popular. Down in Vancouver especially.Nobody has them here probably can't afford them, lol. All I know is that my buddy (86 prelude driver) is very pissed that Pontiac was so brillant, it's almost like they were way ahead of there time. For once he is jealous, hehehe, I just have to finish it all off with the LED lights that funny enough I can only can get at walmart.||||reg||1
